#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Introduction {#1-introduction}"
msgstr "1. Pengenalan {#1-introduction}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This lesson explores modern quantum computing hardware.\n"
msgstr "Pelajaran ini meneroka perkakasan pengkomputeran kuantum moden.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will start by verifying some versions and importing some relevant packages.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan mulakan dengan mengesahkan beberapa versi dan mengimport pakej-pakej yang berkaitan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Backend and Target {#2-backend-and-target}"
msgstr "2. Backend dan Target {#2-backend-and-target}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Qiskit provides an API to obtain the information, both static and dynamic, about a quantum device. We use a Backend instance to interface with a device, which includes a Target instance, an abstract machine model that summarizes the pertinent features such as its instruction set architecture (ISA) and any properties or constraints associated with it.\n"
"Let us use these backend instances to get some of the information you see on the [Compute resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) page\n"
"on IBM Quantum&reg; Platform.   First, we create a backend instance for a device of interest.  In the following, we pick \"ibm_kyoto\" , \"ibm_kawasaki\" or the least busy Eagle machine. Your access to QPUs might differ; update the backend name accordingly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Qiskit menyediakan API untuk mendapatkan maklumat, sama ada statik mahupun dinamik, tentang peranti kuantum. Kita menggunakan contoh Backend untuk berinteraksi dengan peranti, yang merangkumi contoh Target — model mesin abstrak yang meringkaskan ciri-ciri penting seperti seni bina set arahan (ISA) serta sebarang sifat atau kekangan yang berkaitan dengannya.\n"
"Mari gunakan contoh-contoh Backend ini untuk mendapatkan sebahagian maklumat yang Anda lihat pada halaman [Compute resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers)\n"
"di IBM Quantum&reg; Platform. Pertama, kita cipta contoh Backend untuk peranti yang diminati. Dalam contoh berikut, kita pilih \"ibm_kyoto\", \"ibm_kawasaki\" atau mesin Eagle yang paling kurang sibuk. Akses Anda kepada QPU mungkin berbeza; kemaskini nama Backend mengikut keperluan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We start with some basic (static) information about the device.\n"
msgstr "Kita mulakan dengan beberapa maklumat asas (statik) tentang peranti tersebut.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.1 Exercise {#21-exercise}"
msgstr "2.1 Latihan {#21-exercise}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Try to get the basic information about a Heron device, \"ibm_strasbourg\". Try this on your own, but code has been added below for you to check yourself.\n"
msgstr "Cuba dapatkan maklumat asas tentang peranti Heron, \"ibm_strasbourg\". Cuba sendiri dulu, tetapi kod telah disediakan di bawah untuk Anda semak.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.2 Coupling map {#22-coupling-map}"
msgstr "2.2 Peta gandingan {#22-coupling-map}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now draw the coupling map of the device. As you can see, nodes are qubits which are numbered. Edges indicate pairs to which you can directly apply the 2-qubit entangling gate.  The topology is called a \"heavy-hex lattice\".\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita lukis peta gandingan peranti. Seperti yang dapat Anda lihat, nod adalah qubit yang diberi nombor. Tepi menunjukkan pasangan yang boleh dikenakan gate pembelit 2-qubit secara langsung. Topologi ini dipanggil \"kekisi hex berat\" (heavy-hex lattice).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/hardware/extracted-outputs/51b87458-a5e8-4e77-a34d-39fe425a5f01-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/hardware/extracted-outputs/51b87458-a5e8-4e77-a34d-39fe425a5f01-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Qubit properties {#3-qubit-properties}"
msgstr "3. Sifat-sifat qubit {#3-qubit-properties}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Eagle device has 127 qubits.   Let us obtain the properties of some of them.\n"
msgstr "Peranti Eagle mempunyai 127 qubit. Mari dapatkan sifat-sifat sebahagian daripadanya.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us calculate the median of T1 times of the qubits.   Compare the result to the one shown for the device on [IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/).\n"
msgstr "Mari kira median masa T1 bagi qubit-qubit tersebut. Bandingkan hasilnya dengan yang ditunjukkan untuk peranti di [IBM Quantum Platform.](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.1 Exercise {#31-exercise}"
msgstr "3.1 Latihan {#31-exercise}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pease calculate the median of T2 times of the qubits. Try this on your own, but code has been added below for you to check yourself.\n"
msgstr "Kira median masa T2 bagi qubit-qubit tersebut. Cuba sendiri dulu, tetapi kod telah disediakan di bawah untuk Anda semak.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.2 Gate and readout errors {#32-gate-and-readout-errors}"
msgstr "3.2 Ralat get dan bacaan {#32-gate-and-readout-errors}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now turn to gate errors. To begin with, we study the data structure of the target instance. It is a dictionary whose keys are operation names.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita beralih kepada ralat get. Untuk permulaan, kita kaji struktur data bagi contoh Target. Ia adalah kamus yang kuncinya merupakan nama operasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Its values are also dictionaries.  Let us look at some of the items of the value (dictionary) for the 'sx' operation.\n"
msgstr "Nilainya juga merupakan kamus. Mari lihat beberapa item daripada nilai (kamus) untuk operasi 'sx'.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us do the same for the 'ecr' and 'measure' operations.\n"
msgstr "Mari lakukan perkara yang sama untuk operasi 'ecr' dan 'measure'.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As you can see, the errors of readout tend to be larger than those of the 2-qubit operation, which in turn tend to be larger than the 1-qubit operation.\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang dapat Anda lihat, ralat bacaan cenderung lebih besar berbanding operasi 2-qubit, yang seterusnya cenderung lebih besar daripada operasi 1-qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Having understood the data structures, we are ready to calculate the median errors for the 'sx' and the 'ecr' gates. Again, compare the results with the ones shown for the device on [IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/).\n"
msgstr "Setelah memahami struktur data, kita sudah bersedia untuk mengira ralat median bagi gate 'sx' dan 'ecr'. Sekali lagi, bandingkan hasilnya dengan yang ditunjukkan untuk peranti di [IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Appendix {#4-appendix}"
msgstr "4. Lampiran {#4-appendix}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A popular feature of Qiskit is its visualization capability. It includes circuit visualizers, state and distribution visualizers, and target visualizer.   You already used the first two in the previous jupyter notebooks.   Let us use some capabilities of the target visualizer.\n"
msgstr "Salah satu ciri popular Qiskit ialah keupayaan visualisasinya. Ini merangkumi visualizer litar, visualizer keadaan dan taburan, serta visualizer Target. Anda sudah menggunakan dua yang pertama dalam notebook Jupyter sebelumnya. Mari gunakan beberapa keupayaan visualizer Target.\n"

